{"ts":"2026-09-01T07:07:36.300Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"b15b98d619eb46723c158c6c","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"ops-csop"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A case opener sharing a segment with its first arm leaks that arm's binding past esac"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"insideCase is computed for a segment before that segment increments caseDepth, so when a case opener and its first arm occupy one segment the arm boundary is never taken. A binding made in that arm stays visible after esac, and a later unconditional npm publish routed through it is reported as attested even though the arm may not have run."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":0},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["attestation","fail-open","security","supply-chain"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-01T07:07:36.300Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-01T07:07:36.300Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A binding made in a case arm that shares a segment with the case opener is not visible after esac; The auditor refuses the publish in both reported shapes rather than attesting it; Regression tests for both shapes are verified red on revert; The existing sibling-arm and compound-line regressions still pass, and no fleet workflow regresses"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"critical"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"496df3b7afd601c8a210d391d28ea9d20c1ce807208a233e103173d901a59571","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Record the case-arm scope leak found by review on PR 81","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T07:07:37.063Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"b15b98d619eb46723c158c6c","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-01T07:07:37.063Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-01T07:07:37.063Z","author":"claude","text":"Reproduced by execution against 56aa31c. Two shapes are FAIL-OPEN (auditPublishAttestation returns failures=[] and attests the publish):\n\n  case \"$X\" in a) FLAG=--provenance ;; esac\n  npm publish $FLAG\n\n  case \"$X\" in a) FLAG=--provenance ;;\n  esac\n  npm publish $FLAG\n\nTwo neighbouring shapes correctly REFUSE, which localises the defect to the opener sharing a segment with the first arm rather than to case handling generally:\n\n  if true; then case \"$X\" in a) FLAG=--provenance ;; esac; fi   -> refused\n  case \"$X\" in a) FLAG=--provenance ;;& *) : ;; esac            -> refused\n\nNote on my own first attempt: I initially wrote the case with a second arm on its own line and saw it refuse, and nearly recorded Greptile's report as unreproduced. The construction has to put the opener and the first arm in one segment. A single non-reproducing construction is not evidence that a reported fail-open is absent."}]}],"before_hash":"496df3b7afd601c8a210d391d28ea9d20c1ce807208a233e103173d901a59571","after_hash":"a2b278037ce319f198376384cb53f4336db28ae01a9df76fa225c4b036acf923","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
